WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
In 2005, couples in the UK could
first form a civil partnership:

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.070
a legal union, not called marriage.

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.780
From 2014, same-sex couples in
England and Wales could marry.

4
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.190
The law changed.

5
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.520
The ancient texts did not.

6
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:21.900
Believers still open the same pages, and
some reach very different conclusions.

7
00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.760
So if two people who love
each other can marry in law,

8
00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.850
why do believers reading the
same texts still disagree?

9
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.630
In this mission, you'll read one
verse from Leviticus two ways,

10
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.230
and test each reading.

11
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.580
Then you'll map where different
churches stand along a line of views.

12
00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:44.930
Your mission: find out why believers
reading the same texts can still disagree.
